How long the promotion of a replica waits for a follow restoring its heads
when asked, rather than end it: the time the newer snapshot is worth.

The promotion weighs the restore in flight on what it wrote so far: when
what is left would take no longer than this at the throughput seen since it
began, the promotion waits for it, this long at most, and the replica starts
on the snapshot it was restoring. Otherwise, as with the default `0`, the
restore is ended at once, its stages discarded, and the replica starts on
the snapshot it held before.

The `--abort-restore` and `--wait-restore` options of a promotion take over.
